From 46af3b054f1509f988fcfc7b5c9ab528bbb189db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:52:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(browser): press keys with modifiers in a background tab

Only browser_type keystrokes could deliver keys, and only printable text plus
\r for Enter. Tab, Escape, arrows and shortcuts like Ctrl+A had no route.

browser_press_key {target_id, tab_id, key, modifiers?, ref?} sends one
trusted Input.dispatchKeyEvent press under focus emulation, so it works
while the tab or window is in the background. It knows the named editing and
navigation keys, F1-F24 and single characters, sets code and the Windows
virtual-key code, and drops text while Ctrl, Alt or Meta is held so the press
acts as a shortcut. With ref the element is focused first.
