+### Keys
+
+`browser_press_key` presses one key with optional `modifiers` (`alt`, `ctrl`,
+`meta`, `shift`): `Enter`, `Tab`, `Escape`, arrows, `Backspace`, `Delete`,
+`Home`, `End`, `PageUp`, `PageDown`, `F1`-`F24`, `Space`, or one character.
+It uses trusted CDP key events under focus emulation, so it works while the tab
+or window is in the background. With `ref`, that element is focused first;
+without it, the key goes to the page's focused element.
+
+```text
+browser_press_key
+  '{"target_id":"<target>","tab_id":"<tab>","ref":"p4:2",
+    "key":"a","modifiers":["ctrl"],"session":"browser-run-1"}'
+```
+
 ### Background tabs
 
 `browser_open_tab` opens a tab in the bound window without selecting it or
